{"parentUuid":"990db145-ac70-400d-989b-a3a88a9bc587","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a660692b75d21afb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019CZqg9b2WCNKeJCjrNACty","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Optuna 2025 2026 TPE CMA-ES backend release improvements\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - optuna/optuna: A hyperparameter optimization framework · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/optuna/optuna\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · optuna/optuna\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/optuna/optuna/releases\"},{\"title\":\"optuna.samplers.CmaEsSampler — Optuna 4.8.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://optuna.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/samplers/generated/optuna.samplers.CmaEsSampler.html\"},{\"title\":\"Optuna Python Optimizers: TPE CMA-ES Hyperband Pruners Study Viz 2025\",\"url\":\"https://www.johal.in/optuna-python-optimizers-tpe-cma-es-hyperband-pruners-study-viz-2025-3/\"},{\"title\":\"optuna.samplers.CmaEsSampler — Optuna 2.10.1 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://optuna.readthedocs.io/en/v2.10.1/reference/generated/optuna.samplers.CmaEsSampler.html\"},{\"title\":\"CMA-ES Sampler that support IPOP-CMA-ES and BIPOP-CMA-ES | OptunaHub\",\"url\":\"https://hub.optuna.org/samplers/restart_cmaes/\"},{\"title\":\"Optuna - A hyperparameter optimization framework\",\"url\":\"https://optuna.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CMA-ES Sampler | OptunaHub\",\"url\":\"https://hub.optuna.org/samplers/cmaes/\"},{\"title\":\"Release v2.6.0 · optuna/optuna\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/optuna/optuna/releases/tag/v2.6.0\"},{\"title\":\"Announcing Optuna 4.4. We have released version 4.4 of the… | by mamu | Optuna | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/optuna/announcing-optuna-4-4-ece661493126\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are the key findings regarding Optuna releases, TPE, CMA-ES backend, and improvements in 2025-2026:\n\n## Recent Optuna Releases\n\nOptuna 4.7.0 was released on January 19, 2026. Prior to that, Optuna 4.6 was announced on November 10, 2025, and Optuna 4.4.0 was released on June 16, 2025.\n\n## CMA-ES Backend Improvements\n\nA significant improvement in 2025 was addressing a limitation from previous versions. Up until Optuna v4.4, CmaEsSampler could not handle one-dimensional space and fell back to random search, but Optuna v4.5 now allows the CMA-ES algorithm to be used for one-dimensional space.\n\nAdditionally, the CMA-ES-based sampler with restart strategy, which was previously part of the Optuna core, has been migrated to OptunaHub in version 4.4, making it available as a community-maintained module.\n\n## TPE Sampler Improvements\n\nThe TPESampler, Optuna's default sampler, now features simplified arguments (the consider_prior argument has been deprecated) as part of the v4.4 release. Additionally, a visualization feature has been added, allowing users to see how the acquisition function of the default TPESampler evolves as trials progress.\n\n## Future Improvements (v5 Roadmap)\n\nIn Optuna v5, they will improve Optuna's default optimization algorithm and its options to enhance performance and usability.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"bc699ff5-b7d0-43d9-a558-c7eb67f31e04","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:53.773Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"990db145-ac70-400d-989b-a3a88a9bc587","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a1d1987d-64d9-491d-89d0-2617199880bc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a660692b75d21afb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HTzuat4487nNtdXJhXRdkd","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Hyperopt maintenance status 2025 last release abandoned\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"hyperopt - Python Package Health Analysis | Snyk\",\"url\":\"https://snyk.io/advisor/python/hyperopt\"},{\"title\":\"Hyperopt Documentation\",\"url\":\"http://hyperopt.github.io/hyperopt/\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · hyperopt/hyperopt\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/hyperopt/hyperopt/releases\"},{\"title\":\"hyperopt · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/hyperopt/\"},{\"title\":\"Hyperopt - Freqtrade\",\"url\":\"https://www.freqtrade.io/en/stable/hyperopt/\"},{\"title\":\"Issues · hyperopt/hyperopt\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/hyperopt/hyperopt/issues\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - hyperopt/hyperopt: Distributed Asynchronous Hyperparameter Optimization in Python · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/hyperopt/hyperopt\"},{\"title\":\"FMin · hyperopt/hyperopt Wiki · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/hyperopt/hyperopt/wiki/FMin\"},{\"title\":\"Hyperopt best practices and troubleshooting - Azure Databricks | Microsoft Learn\",\"url\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/databricks/machine-learning/automl-hyperparam-tuning/hyperopt-best-practices\"},{\"title\":\"HyperOS 3.0 Update Tracker: Eligible Devices and Expected Release Dates (2025–2026)\",\"url\":\"https://www.hyperskinz.com/2026/02/hyperos-30-update-tracker-eligible.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Hyperopt's maintenance status:\n\n## Maintenance Status\n\nHyperopt's maintenance is classified as Sustainable according to Snyk's analysis as of October 2025. However, there are significant concerns about active development:\n\nHyperopt hasn't seen any new versions released to PyPI in the past 12 months and could be considered as a discontinued project or one that receives low attention from its maintainers.\n\nAdditionally, in the past month no pull request activity or change in issues status has been detected for the GitHub repository.\n\n## Status from Microsoft/Azure Databricks\n\nIt's worth noting that the open-source version of Hyperopt is no longer being maintained, according to Microsoft's Azure Databricks documentation. Azure Databricks recommends using either Optuna for single-node optimization or RayTune as alternatives.\n\n## Summary\n\nWhile the project hasn't been formally abandoned, it appears to be in a state of minimal maintenance with no recent releases and little ongoing activity. This makes it a project that may have reliability and compatibility concerns going forward.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8e814b04-12c1-4656-97c8-afa0dea051fb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:54.823Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a1d1987d-64d9-491d-89d0-2617199880bc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"38959770-19ef-4d96-a84d-00c8a4d83a02","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a660692b75d21afb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HvFyX2nFjWGPc4rD3tNj86","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SMAC3 AutoML Bayesian optimization 2025 vs Optuna comparison\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SMAC3 Registered on OptunaHub. SMAC3, a SOTA Bayesian optimization… | by difandeng | Optuna | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/optuna/smac3-registered-on-optunahub-4fb9e90855cb\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - automl/SMAC3: SMAC3: A Versatile Bayesian Optimization Package for Hyperparameter Optimization · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/automl/SMAC3\"},{\"title\":\"SMAC3 | OptunaHub\",\"url\":\"https://hub.optuna.org/samplers/smac_sampler/\"},{\"title\":\"Bayesian Optimization | OptunaHub\",\"url\":\"https://hub.optuna.org/tags/bayesian-optimization/\"},{\"title\":\"A Comparison of AutoML Hyperparameter Optimization Tools for Tabular Data by\",\"url\":\"https://etd.ohiolink.edu/acprod/odb_etd/ws/send_file/send?accession=ysu1682941140945486&disposition=inline\"},{\"title\":\"AutoML | SMAC3: A Versatile Bayesian Optimization Package for Hyperparameter Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.automl.org/hpo-overview/hpo-tools/smac/\"},{\"title\":\"Samplers | OptunaHub\",\"url\":\"https://hub.optuna.org/samplers/\"},{\"title\":\"An improved hyperparameter optimization framework for AutoML systems using evolutionary algorithms - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10036546/\"},{\"title\":\"AutoML | Overview of HPO Tools\",\"url\":\"https://www.automl.org/hpo-overview/hpo-tools/hpo-packages/\"},{\"title\":\"A Comparative study of Hyper-Parameter Optimization Tools Shashank Shekhar\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2201.06433\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about SMAC3 and Optuna for Bayesian optimization:\n\n## Overview\n\nSMAC offers a robust and flexible framework for Bayesian Optimization to support users in determining well-performing hyperparameter configurations for their machine learning algorithms, datasets and applications. Optuna is an automatic HPO framework that allows to dynamically construct the search space.\n\n## Key Differences\n\n**SMAC3 Strengths:**\n- SMAC3 is well known for optimizing complex and structured spaces (e.g., for optimizing entire ML pipelines) based on RF-surrogate models\n- The main core consists of Bayesian Optimization in combination with an aggressive racing mechanism to efficiently decide which of two configurations performs better\n\n**Optuna Strengths:**\n- Optuna implements both Bayesian optimization and evolutionary algorithms\n- In terms of time, Optuna has the better performance in all the datasets except semeion\n\n## Integration\n\nInterestingly, the Optuna team collaborated with AutoML.org this time, having led to a SMAC3-based sampler contribution to OptunaHub. This means SMAC3 is now available as a sampler within Optuna itself, allowing users to compare both approaches directly.\n\nThe search results don't contain specific 2025 benchmarks comparing the two frameworks, but the most recent information (from February 2025) shows they can be integrated and compared within the same framework.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"88e24a2b-95e2-4cae-9524-2dbbf05c774b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:55.576Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"38959770-19ef-4d96-a84d-00c8a4d83a02","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0e2f59d5-0f97-4ec0-8661-cc273e57b7d9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a660692b75d21afb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018Ak13CdpU69NzjAyK7QsHY","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"BoTorch Ax Meta Bayesian optimization 2025 hyperparameter tuning\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Introduction | BoTorch\",\"url\":\"https://botorch.org/docs/introduction/\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Optimization With Ax, an Open Platform for Adaptive Experimentation - Engineering at Meta\",\"url\":\"https://engineering.fb.com/2025/11/18/open-source/efficient-optimization-ax-open-platform-adaptive-experimentation/\"},{\"title\":\"Open-sourcing new AI tools for adaptive experimentation\",\"url\":\"https://ai.meta.com/blog/open-sourcing-ax-and-botorch-new-ai-tools-for-adaptive-experimentation/\"},{\"title\":\"[1912.05686] Bayesian Hyperparameter Optimization with BoTorch, GPyTorch and Ax\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.05686\"},{\"title\":\"Meta releases Ax 1.0 for automated machine learning optimization\",\"url\":\"https://ppc.land/meta-releases-ax-1-0-for-automated-machine-learning-optimization/\"},{\"title\":\"Meta's Optimization Platform Ax 1.0 Streamlines LLM and System Optimization - InfoQ\",\"url\":\"https://www.infoq.com/news/2025/12/ax-hyperparameter-optimization/\"},{\"title\":\"Using BoTorch with Ax | BoTorch\",\"url\":\"https://botorch.org/docs/botorch_and_ax/\"},{\"title\":\"Bayesian Hyperparameter Optimization with BoTorch, GPyTorch and Ax\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1912.05686\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - meta-pytorch/botorch: Bayesian optimization in PyTorch · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/meta-pytorch/botorch\"},{\"title\":\"Bayesian Optimization for Hyperparameters Tuning in Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2410.21886v1\"}]\n\n## Search Results Summary\n\nBased on your search query about BoTorch, Ax, Meta, Bayesian optimization, and hyperparameter tuning in 2025, here are the key findings:\n\n### Overview of BoTorch and Ax\n\nBoTorch is best used in tandem with Ax, Facebook's open-source adaptive experimentation platform, which provides an easy-to-use interface for defining, managing and running sequential experiments. Ax relies on BoTorch for its implementation of Bayesian optimization components.\n\n### Recent Developments (2025)\n\nMeta released Ax 1.0 on November 18, 2025, coinciding with publication of the platform's technical paper in AutoML 2025's ABCD Track, following years of internal deployment and development at Meta.\n\n### Hyperparameter Tuning Applications\n\nAx has been successfully applied to traditional machine learning tasks, such as hyperparameter optimization and architecture search. Thousands of developers at Meta use Ax for tasks like hyperparameter optimization and architecture search for AI models.\n\n### Technical Approach\n\nAx employs Bayesian optimization and machine learning to automate complex experimentation processes, using Gaussian processes as surrogate models and expected improvement acquisition functions to identify optimal configurations across systems with hundreds of tunable parameters.\n\n### Key Features\n\nMeta researchers emphasize Ax's expressive API, which enables exploration of complex search spaces and handling multiple objectives, constraints, and noisy observations. Ax can also evaluate distinct configurations in parallel and halt evaluation at any time. A key benefit of Ax is that it provides sensible defaults, allowing practitioners to leverage advanced techniques without needing to be optimization experts.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"714c599f-3e8c-4ceb-a242-9cfdaeb65e9b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:56.960Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0e2f59d5-0f97-4ec0-8661-cc273e57b7d9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
