{"parentUuid":"59aae7a0-51e9-497b-bba8-12674d24056b","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a660692b75d21afb7","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0139EAaAbWznnZ7eGB35a7eW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KWJct7wrNyGiVJ64DrCqS7","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"multi-objective hyperparameter optimization Optuna NSGA-II BoTorch comparison 2025"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5244,"cache_read_input_tokens":20395,"output_tokens":323,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5244},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":323,"cache_read_input_tokens":20395,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5244,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5244,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyUNwL5DfnxMrx94GWd","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"46e00190-8645-49a8-b7d9-2ec1deb8b3b3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:02.242Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c2471e90-bc38-4380-bbf7-b142747f6be3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a660692b75d21afb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SdXN3nkKitg1U9mzvFh21Y","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Nevergrad gradient-free optimization 2025 benchmark hyperparameter\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Nevergrad - A gradient-free optimization platform — nevergrad documentation\",\"url\":\"https://facebookresearch.github.io/nevergrad/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - LaurentMazare/nevergrad: A Python toolbox for performing gradient-free optimization\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/LaurentMazare/nevergrad\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - zaffnet/nevergrad: A Python toolbox for performing gradient-free optimization\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/zaffnet/nevergrad\"},{\"title\":\"Nevergrad: An open source tool for derivative-free optimization - Engineering at Meta\",\"url\":\"https://engineering.fb.com/2018/12/20/ai-research/nevergrad/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - facebookresearch/nevergrad: A Python toolbox for performing gradient-free optimization · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/facebookresearch/nevergrad\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - sailfish009/nevergrad: A Python toolbox for performing gradient-free optimization\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/sailfish009/nevergrad\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - carsondahlberg/nevergrad: A Python toolbox for performing gradient-free optimization\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/carsondahlberg/nevergrad\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - 42MachineLearning/nevergrad: A Python toolbox for performing gradient-free optimization\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/42MachineLearning/nevergrad\"},{\"title\":\"nevergrad · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/nevergrad/0.2.1/\"},{\"title\":\"How to perform optimization — nevergrad documentation\",\"url\":\"https://facebookresearch.github.io/nevergrad/optimization.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Nevergrad:\n\n## Overview\n\nNevergrad is a Python 3.6+ library developed by Facebook Research (now Meta) for gradient-free optimization. Nevergrad offers an extensive collection of algorithms that do not require gradient computation and presents them in a standard ask-and-tell Python framework. It also includes testing and evaluation tools.\n\n## Applications\n\nIn machine learning, Nevergrad can be used to tune hyperparameters such as learning rate, momentum, weight decay (possibly per layer), dropout, and layer parameters for each part of a deep network, or others.\n\n## Benchmarking and Hyperparameter Optimization\n\nThe benchmark tools aim at providing a way to evaluate optimizers on a large range of settings. They provide a way to run the optimizers on all settings and record the results, as well as ways to plot the results of the experiments. Experiment plans are described in nevergrad.benchmark.experiments. Each experiment plan is a generator yielding different Experiment instances (defining function and optimizer settings).\n\n## Key Optimizers for Hyperparameter Tuning\n\nNgIohTuned is a \"meta\"-optimizer which adapts to the provided settings (budget, number of workers, parametrization) and should therefore be a good default. TwoPointsDE is excellent in many cases, including very high num_workers.\n\nThe search results don't contain specific information about 2025 benchmark results, but the framework continues to provide comprehensive tools for gradient-free optimization and hyperparameter tuning across various problem types.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c27173e8-1e73-4f47-abb3-5498e9da6460","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:06.773Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c2471e90-bc38-4380-bbf7-b142747f6be3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b36ac1d8-cbee-443c-9082-fc1d9131132d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a660692b75d21afb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UxuRBD855QuMeJ9XbAGZuv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT solver hyperparameter tuning benchmark Optuna SMAC SAT\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-autotune: WIP: Tune the hyperparameters of Google's OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver for specific models · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-autotune\"},{\"title\":\"SMAC3 | OptunaHub\",\"url\":\"https://hub.optuna.org/samplers/smac_sampler/\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"A Comparative study of Hyper-Parameter Optimization Tools Shashank Shekhar\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2201.06433\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"DeepHyper: A Python Package for Massively Parallel ...\",\"url\":\"https://joss.theoj.org/papers/10.21105/joss.07975.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Optuna - A hyperparameter optimization framework\",\"url\":\"https://optuna.org/\"},{\"title\":\"The Conﬁgurable SAT Solver Challenge (CSSC)\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.ubc.ca/~kevinlb/papers/2017-AIJ-CSSC.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"cp-sat · GitHub Topics · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/topics/cp-sat\"},{\"title\":\"Better Understandings and Configurations in MaxSAT Local Search Solvers via Anytime Performance Analysis\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2403.06568v1\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found regarding CP-SAT solver hyperparameter tuning with Optuna and SMAC:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**CP-SAT and Optuna Integration:**\ncpsat-autotune is a Python library designed to optimize the hyperparameters of Google's OR-Tools CP-SAT solver for specific problem instances, leveraging the optuna optimization library to systematically explore and suggest optimal hyperparameter configurations.\n\n**How cpsat-autotune Works:**\ncpsat-autotune uses the optuna library to perform hyperparameter tuning on a preselected set of parameters, and the output of optuna is then further refined with significance evaluation of certain parameters, identifying the most significant changes to the default configuration.\n\n**Comparison of Hyperparameter Optimization Tools:**\nThe search results include a comparative study of optimization tools. For the CASH problem benchmark, Optuna is a good option considering the trade-off between runtime and performance score, while for the MLP problem, HyperOpt performs better.\n\nRegarding SMAC specifically: SMAC offers a robust and flexible framework for Bayesian Optimization with its main core consisting of Bayesian Optimization in combination with an aggressive racing mechanism to efficiently decide which of two configurations performs better.\n\n**Practical Comparison:**\nOptuna uses the TPE sampler with default arguments while SMAC uses default parameters via the OptunaHub SMAC sampler.\n\nThe results show that both Optuna and SMAC are actively used for hyperparameter optimization tasks, with SMAC also being available as a sampler within Optuna's ecosystem through OptunaHub.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0bf45178-6f44-4018-b879-f633349db4b9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:08.357Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b36ac1d8-cbee-443c-9082-fc1d9131132d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"59aae7a0-51e9-497b-bba8-12674d24056b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a660692b75d21afb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FmqwoNx7gqwsVRz4LQ8hK5","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SMAC vs Optuna SAT solver configuration AClib SATzilla 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SMAC Generic Wrapper - AClib\",\"url\":\"https://aclib.net/smac/tutorial/genericwrapper/\"},{\"title\":\"Automatic solver configuration using SMAC\",\"url\":\"https://www.automl.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/07/SAT_Industrial_16_AC.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - sfalkner/SpySMAC: A tool for automatic SAT solver configuration using SMAC combined with extensive analysis.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/sfalkner/SpySMAC\"},{\"title\":\"Automated Configuration and Selection of SAT Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.ubc.ca/~kevinlb/papers/2021-SAT-handbook-chapter.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SMAC3 | OptunaHub\",\"url\":\"https://hub.optuna.org/samplers/smac_sampler/\"},{\"title\":\"Practical, Utilitarian Algorithm Configuration\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.14683v1\"},{\"title\":\"Revisiting SATZilla Features in 2024 Hadar Shavit #\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol305-sat2024/LIPIcs.SAT.2024.27/LIPIcs.SAT.2024.27.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Automatic solver conﬁguration using SMAC\",\"url\":\"http://www.ml4aad.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/07/SAT_Industrial_16_AC.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"AClib\",\"url\":\"https://aclib.net/\"},{\"title\":\"Spy SMAC Automated Configuration and Performance Analysis of SAT Solvers - SpySMAC: Automated - Studocu\",\"url\":\"https://www.studocu.com/row/document/beijing-normal-university/the-study-of-anything/spy-smac-automated-configuration-and-performance-analysis-of-sat-solvers/52945547\"}]\n\nI've found relevant information about SAT solver configuration tools and methods. Here's what the search results reveal:\n\n## SMAC for SAT Solver Configuration\n\nSMAC is a tool for automatic SAT solver configuration combined with extensive analysis. SMAC offers a robust and flexible framework for Bayesian Optimization, with the main core consisting of Bayesian Optimization in combination with an aggressive racing mechanism to efficiently decide which of two configurations performs better.\n\n## Comparison with Other Methods\n\nSMAC 3 has been compared to other configuration methods using the ACLib library of algorithm configuration benchmarks in scenarios consisting of four different SAT solvers and 20 different instance sets. SMAC performed statistically significantly better than ParamILS in 11 of 17 cases.\n\n## SATzilla and Features\n\nSATzilla features are commonly used in model-based algorithm configuration where hyperparameters of SAT solvers are optimized, and SMAC successfully used the SATzilla features to optimize the performance of a wide range of SAT solvers on various benchmarks.\n\n## Optuna Integration\n\nSMAC is available as a sampler for Optuna and is maintained by the SMAC team at automl.org, allowing users to integrate SMAC's configuration capabilities into Optuna workflows.\n\nThe search results don't contain specific comparisons between SMAC and Optuna directly, or detailed information specific to 2025 benchmarks. Would you like me to search for more recent comparative studies or specific benchmark results?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5027f322-5b02-4bc1-ad93-7d2408abe874","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:08.811Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"59aae7a0-51e9-497b-bba8-12674d24056b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"46e00190-8645-49a8-b7d9-2ec1deb8b3b3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a660692b75d21afb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KWJct7wrNyGiVJ64DrCqS7","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"multi-objective hyperparameter optimization Optuna NSGA-II BoTorch comparison 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Announcing Optuna 3.0 (Part 2). The third major version release of… | by mamu | Optuna | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/optuna/optuna-3-part-2-3d64bca63573\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · optuna/optuna\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/optuna/optuna/releases\"},{\"title\":\"AutoSampler: Full Support for Multi-Objective & Constrained Optimization | by Yoshihiko Ozaki | Optuna | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/optuna/autosampler-full-support-for-multi-objective-constrained-optimization-c1c4fc957ba2\"},{\"title\":\"Samplers | OptunaHub\",\"url\":\"https://hub.optuna.org/samplers/\"},{\"title\":\"Optuna - A hyperparameter optimization framework\",\"url\":\"https://optuna.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Master Hyperparameter Optimization with Optuna: A Complete Guide [Part 1] | by Mihir Shah | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@mdshah930/master-hyperparameter-optimization-with-optuna-a-complete-guide-89971b799b0a\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - optuna/optuna: A hyperparameter optimization framework · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/optuna/optuna\"},{\"title\":\"Multi-Objective Hyperparameter Optimization in Machine Learning—An Overview | ACM Transactions on Evolutionary Learning and Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3610536\"},{\"title\":\"Comparison table for samplers · Issue #2622 · optuna/optuna\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/optuna/optuna/issues/2622\"},{\"title\":\"Multiobjective optimization with constraints, (MO)TPE vs NSGA-II, etc. · optuna/optuna · Discussion #5259\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/optuna/optuna/discussions/5259\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about multi-objective hyperparameter optimization with Optuna, NSGA-II, and BoTorch in 2025:\n\n## Recent Developments in Optuna (2025)\n\nOptuna v4.4 extended GPSampler to support multi-objective optimization problems, with applications expected in material design, experimental design, and high-cost hyperparameter optimization. GPSampler can be easily integrated and performs well against the existing BoTorchSampler.\n\nAutoSampler dynamically switches between four powerful methods based on problem characteristics: GPSampler, TPESampler, NSGAIISampler, and NSGAIIISampler. This automatic selection allows it to find better solutions by adapting its strategy to the task at hand.\n\n## NSGA-II Performance Improvements\n\nWhile NSGA-II performs well for categorical parameters by default, it often does not perform well enough for floating point parameters, but with the new crossover option, NSGA-II performs well on real variables. Comparison figures show NSGA-II with newly implemented crossover, existing NSGA-II, existing BoTorch method, and another NSGA-II implementation on the NAS bench 101 problem after 140 trials.\n\n## Available Algorithms\n\nTwo new multi-objective samplers—SPEA-II and HypE—have been introduced to OptunaHub, where SPEA-II is an improved multi-objective evolutionary algorithm differing from NSGA-II in its selection mechanism, and HypE is a fast, hypervolume-based evolutionary algorithm for many-objective optimization.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cd323f4a-396b-46fb-993a-bd1e38d13d76","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:09.480Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"46e00190-8645-49a8-b7d9-2ec1deb8b3b3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cd323f4a-396b-46fb-993a-bd1e38d13d76","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a660692b75d21afb7","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01QLLdmSTEvY1KmrxBodtRrm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough material. Let me synthesize the findings into a structured ≤800 word report.\n\n---\n\n# Optuna vs SMAC3 vs Hyperopt vs BoTorch vs Random vs Grid — CP-SAT 调参选型\n\n## 1. Optuna 2024-2026 进展\n\n最新 4.7.0（2026-01），4.4-4.6 在 2025 集中迭代。**重点动作**：\n- **TPE**（默认 sampler）简化参数（`consider_prior` 弃用），加了 acquisition function 可视化\n- **CMA-ES** 4.5 起支持 1 维空间（之前 fallback 到随机）；带 restart 的 IPOP/BIPOP-CMA-ES 移到 OptunaHub\n- **GPSampler** 4.4 起支持多目标，性能对标 BoTorchSampler\n- **AutoSampler** 自动在 GP/TPE/NSGA-II/NSGA-III 之间切换（新功能，2025）\n- **OptunaHub** 把 SMAC3、SPEA-II、HypE 都接进来当 sampler 用\n\n## 2. SMAC3 现状\n\nAutoML.org 维护，是 SAT solver 配置圈的**事实标准工具**（ACLib benchmark、SATzilla 特征都默认配 SMAC）。核心是 RF surrogate + Bayesian optimization + **aggressive racing**（早期淘汰差配置，关键优势）。在 ACLib 的 4 SAT solver × 20 instance 对比里，SMAC 比 ParamILS 在 17 场里赢 11 场。**2025 关键事件**：SMAC 团队和 Optuna 团队合作，把 SMAC3 做成 OptunaHub sampler，可以在 Optuna 框架里直接调用。\n\n## 3. Hyperopt 已半死\n\nSnyk 标 \"Sustainable\" 但**过去 12 个月零 PyPI release**，最近一个月零 PR / issue 活动。Microsoft Azure Databricks 官方文档**已明说 \"open-source Hyperopt is no longer maintained\"**，推荐用 Optuna 或 RayTune 替代。结论：不要选。\n\n## 4. BoTorch / Ax (Meta)\n\n**Ax 1.0 在 2025-11-18 发布**（重大事件），论文进 AutoML 2025 ABCD Track。BoTorch 是底层 GP-BO 引擎，Ax 是上层平台。Meta 内部数千开发者在用。强项：\n- GP surrogate + EI acquisition，**搜索空间可超百维**\n- 原生支持多目标、约束、噪声观测\n- 并行评估、随时停止\n\n弱项：上手成本高于 Optuna；GP 在 trial 数 >500 后扩展性变差（CP-SAT 调参典型 budget 在这个量级）。\n\n## 5. Nevergrad\n\nMeta 出品，**gradient-free 算法库**（CMA-ES、DE、PSO 等几十种）。核心组件 `NgIohTuned` 是 meta-optimizer（自动选算法）。强项是离散/混合空间和高 num_workers 并行。弱项：缺贝叶斯 surrogate 模型，CP-SAT 这种**单次评估贵**的场景效率不如 SMAC/BoTorch。更适合 budget 大（>10k trials）的场景。\n\n## 6. SAT solver benchmark 实证\n\n- SMAC 在 SAT 圈是 SOTA，SATzilla / SpySMAC / 算法配置文献几乎清一色 SMAC\n- cpsat-autotune（你 Round 5 在调研的）用的是 **Optuna TPE**，因为它对 CP-SAT 这种\"参数 ~30 个、连续+分类混合\"的场景上手快\n- 2022 ArXiv 比较研究：CASH benchmark 上 Optuna 综合最佳（runtime + score），MLP 上 Hyperopt 略好；**没有专门 CP-SAT 调参 benchmark**（这是 d-krupke 自己在 cpsat-primer 里做的工作）\n\n## 7. 168h budget 适配\n\n我们的 budget 量级：典型 50-300 trials（每个 trial 跑一次完整 campaign 子问题，单次几分钟到几十分钟）。\n- **<100 trials** → BoTorch/Ax（GP 在小样本下信息利用率最高）或 SMAC3（racing 帮你早停烂配置，省一半时间）\n- **100-1000 trials** → **Optuna TPE 性价比最高**，cpsat-autotune 已经验证\n- **>1000 trials** → Nevergrad / CMA-ES\n\n我们落在第二档。**SMAC racing 的吸引力在这里**：CP-SAT 调参的痛点是慢配置吃光预算，racing 可以在中位时间就杀掉差配置。\n\n## 8. 多目标支持（time + memory）\n\n| 工具 | 多目标 | 实战推荐 |\n|---|---|---|\n| Optuna | NSGAII / NSGAIII / GPSampler / MOTPE | 成熟 |\n| SMAC3 | ParEGO 风格，原生支持 | 成熟 |\n| BoTorch/Ax | qEHVI / qNEHVI（GP-based，最强） | **理论最优** |\n| Hyperopt | 不支持 | × |\n| Nevergrad | 部分支持 | 一般 |\n\n时间+内存这种**目标量纲差异大**的，BoTorch 的 qNEHVI 处理最干净，但工程复杂度也最高。\n\n---\n\n## 换 Optuna 之外的工具值得吗\n\n**不值得直接换，但值得加一个 SMAC3 sampler 做 A/B**。理由：\n\n1. **不换 Optuna 主框架**：Optuna 是 cpsat-autotune 已验证路径，搜索空间定义、checkpoint、可视化全套生态 OK。换框架本身的工程成本就吃掉一周。\n2. **直接通过 OptunaHub 加 SMAC3 sampler**：一行 import 替换，把 SMAC 的 RF + racing 接进来，在同一套 trial 数据上对比 TPE。这是 2025 年 AutoML 团队和 Optuna 团队联合做的官方路径，零迁移成本。\n3. **Ax/BoTorch 留给\"小 budget 高价值\"场景**：比如最终 168h 跑前的\"最后 50 trial 精修\"，用 GP-BO 比 TPE 信息利用率高。\n\n**操作建议**：保留 cpsat-autotune 的 Optuna TPE 作为基线；在 Lane B 加一个 SMAC3 sampler 实验（同 budget、同搜索空间、同评估函数，对比最终 area / min_side）；Ax/BoTorch 列入\"如果 SMAC3 也不显著优于 TPE 才上\"的 Tier 2。Hyperopt 和 Grid 直接 ban，Random 留作 sanity baseline。\n\nSources:\n- [Optuna releases](https://github.com/optuna/optuna/releases)\n- [Announcing Optuna 4.4](https://medium.com/optuna/announcing-optuna-4-4-ece661493126)\n- [SMAC3 Registered on OptunaHub](https://medium.com/optuna/smac3-registered-on-optunahub-4fb9e90855cb)\n- [SMAC3 GitHub](https://github.com/automl/SMAC3)\n- [Automatic solver configuration using SMAC (SAT industrial)](https://www.automl.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/07/SAT_Industrial_16_AC.pdf)\n- [Hyperopt Snyk health analysis](https://snyk.io/advisor/python/hyperopt)\n- [Azure Databricks Hyperopt deprecation note](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/databricks/machine-learning/automl-hyperparam-tuning/hyperopt-best-practices)\n- [Meta Ax 1.0 announcement](https://engineering.fb.com/2025/11/18/open-source/efficient-optimization-ax-open-platform-adaptive-experimentation/)\n- [Ax 1.0 InfoQ writeup](https://www.infoq.com/news/2025/12/ax-hyperparameter-optimization/)\n- [Nevergrad documentation](https://facebookresearch.github.io/nevergrad/)\n- [cpsat-autotune (d-krupke)](https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-autotune)\n- [A Comparative Study of HPO Tools (arXiv 2201.06433)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2201.06433)\n- [AutoSampler: Multi-Objective & Constrained](https://medium.com/optuna/autosampler-full-support-for-multi-objective-constrained-optimization-c1c4fc957ba2)\n- [Configurable SAT Solver Challenge](https://www.cs.ubc.ca/~kevinlb/papers/2017-AIJ-CSSC.pdf)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5439,"cache_read_input_tokens":25639,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5439,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyVJCbsCmR1cnMkpHE8","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"df7cc508-440f-4bc4-82d1-63ee638836e9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:12:06.727Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
